  "term": "estrogen replacement therapy",
  "definition": "Estrogen replacement therapy is the use of estrogen as a replacement hormone treatment. In the supplied source, it is described as being associated in population studies with a lower risk of Alzheimer’s disease, but a higher risk of breast cancer and some cardiovascular disorders.",
